  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is primarily driven by mid-morning liquidity decay (entries between 10:35 and 11:10 IST) where low-conviction breakouts immediately mean-revert and trigger the tight 0.45% stop loss. Furthermore, Trades #4 (ICICIBANK) and #10 (AXISBANK) exited in gross profit via trailing stop/breakeven mechanisms, yet flipped to net losses due to transaction fee drag eroding micro-gains. Lastly, a single-day directional correlation cluster on 2026-10-22 resulted in four simultaneous long failures across high-beta sectors.",
    "learning": "In NSE cash equities, setting a breakeven trigger at 1.0R without sufficient target velocity subjects trades to normal 5-minute intraday noise retracements, converting winning directional reads into fee-induced net losses; simultaneously, mid-day entries require significantly higher volume confirmation (\u22652.4x) and wider structural stops (\u22650.55%) to filter out institutional stop-runs.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.35,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.4,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.25,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #73 Quantitative Review & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing revealed severe fee drag (\u20b955.64 fees vs \u20b910.16 gross profit) and mid-morning stop-out clusters between 10:30 and 11:15 IST. Forensics on ICICIBANK and AXISBANK demonstrated that triggering breakeven stops at `1.0R` prematurely choked winning trades during routine pullbacks, turning gross profits into net fee losses. To establish positive expectancy, `min_sl_pct` is widened to **0.55%** to survive NSE 5-minute order-book noise, `breakeven_trigger_r` is pushed to **1.25R** to allow trades room to breathe before locking stops, `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` is raised to **2.40x** to eliminate low-liquidity mid-day false breakouts, and `min_target_pct` is scaled to **1.35%** to ensure gross winners easily clear statutory brokerage and STT hurdles."
